# Caddy block to ADD to /opt/app/Caddyfile on the Hetzner VPS.
#
# Place INSIDE the existing `{$DOMAIN:localhost} { … }` block, BEFORE the
# existing `reverse_proxy app:3000 { … }` (which catches `/`). Caddy
# matches `handle` directives in source order; the `/cards*` matcher must
# be first so it wins over the catch-all.

# --- snip ---

# Match `/cards`, `/cards/`, and `/cards/anything` and forward with the
# path INTACT to the cards container (named `cards`, port 3000) over the
# shared `app_web` network. The Next.js server is built with
# basePath=/cards so it already expects requests under that prefix — we
# don't strip. `handle` (vs `handle_path`) preserves the URL path.
handle /cards* {
    reverse_proxy cards:3000 {
        header_up Host {host}
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
        header_up X-Forwarded-For {remote_host}
        header_up X-Forwarded-Proto {scheme}
    }
}

# --- /snip ---

# Reload Caddy after editing:
#   cd /opt/app && docker compose exec caddy caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
